Industry Example (DevOps)

A team developing an Internet Banking application typically follows this workflow:

main (Production)
        │
        ├── feature-UPI
        ├── feature-NetBanking
        ├── bugfix-Login
        ├── hotfix-Production
        └── release-v2.5

After code review and successful CI/CD testing, the approved branch is merged into main for deployment.

Key takeaway: Branches enable safe, parallel development while keeping the production code in main stable and deployable.
